evidence.text:
Expected complete reply shape, using an authored offline example:
{
  "contract": "ocr-productive-repair-text-reply-v3",
  "readings": [
    {
      "corrected_text": "The Committee on Appropriations recommended non-concurrence.",
      "coverage": "complete",
      "paragraph_alias": "P1",
      "reason": null
    }
  ],
  "unit_id": "S5"
}

The updated prompt now explicitly says: for a complete reading, return the entire text and a JSON null reason, without a completion comment. For an incomplete reading, return no text and explain the uncertainty.

The new response schema expresses those same two alternatives. The reply fields and host checks stay the same. A prompt from one version cannot be paired with the other version’s schema.

Unchanged actual reply: rejected by the new schema and by the host, for the same comment-field inconsistency.

Authored complete example above: accepted by both checks, with an unreviewed text proposal linked to the original paragraph. This is an offline example, not a new AI response.

Authored uncertain example:
{
  "contract": "ocr-productive-repair-text-reply-v3",
  "readings": [
    {
      "corrected_text": null,
      "coverage": "incomplete",
      "paragraph_alias": "P1",
      "reason": "Last word is unclear."
    }
  ],
  "unit_id": "S5"
}

Actual software outcome for that uncertain example: both checks accept the uncertainty, no text proposal is produced, and its status remains unresolved. Empty or contradictory combinations are rejected. No model call was made during this fix.
